{
  "meta": {
    "setup": [
      "Add a Jitterflow endpoint pointing at your ERP's order-import URL, paced to its rate limit.",
      "Select your Jitterflow API credential on both Jitterflow nodes and paste the endpoint key.",
      "Create a Crypto credential holding your Shopify webhook signing secret and select it on Compute signature.",
      "Select a Slack credential and channel, activate, and register the production URL in Shopify for orders/create."
    ],
    "description": "Verifies each Shopify orders/create webhook's HMAC, maps the order to an ERP import shape and queues it in Jitterflow, which delivers to the ERP at its rate limit with retries and idempotency. A daily lane posts a Slack summary of orders that landed in the dead-letter queue."
  },
  "name": "Sync Shopify orders to a rate-limited ERP with signature checks and Slack failure alerts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0101-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 600,
        "height": 1100,
        "content": "## Sync Shopify orders to a rate-limited ERP with signature checks and Slack failure alerts\n\n### Who's it for\nShopify stores whose ERP or order-management API has a rate limit. A flash sale fires one `orders/create` webhook per order, and calling the ERP directly turns that burst into 429 errors and missing orders.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Shopify order created** receives each order. **Compute signature** and **Signature matches?** check Shopify's HMAC header and answer 401 to anything unsigned.\n2. **Map order to ERP format** keeps what an ERP import needs: order number, customer, ship-to, totals and one line per SKU.\n3. **Queue order for the ERP** hands it to [Jitterflow](https://jitterflow.io), which delivers orders to the ERP one at a time at the endpoint's cadence, with retries. The Shopify order ID is the idempotency key, so Shopify's retries never import an order twice.\n4. **Acknowledge Shopify** answers 200 only after the order is queued.\n5. Every morning, the bottom lane reads Jitterflow's dead-letter queue (DLQ) and posts one Slack summary of orders the ERP rejected. No failures, no message.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Jitterflow account and API key. The free Developer plan works.\n- The `n8n-nodes-jitterflow` community node. It is verified by n8n, so it's available on n8n Cloud; on self-hosted n8n, install it from **Settings \u2192 Community Nodes**.\n- Shopify admin access and a Slack workspace.\n\n### How to set up\n1. In Jitterflow, add an endpoint whose destination URL is your ERP's order-import API. Set **Deliver one every** to the ERP's limit and put its API key in **Auth header**.\n2. Create a **Jitterflow API** credential, select it on both Jitterflow nodes, and paste the endpoint key into **Endpoint Key**.\n3. Create a **Crypto** credential whose **Hmac Secret** is your Shopify webhook signing secret, and select it on **Compute signature**.\n4. Select a Slack credential and channel on **Alert the ops channel**.\n5. Activate the workflow and add its production URL in Shopify as an `orders/create` webhook in JSON format.\n\n### How to customize\n- Change the fields in **Map order to ERP format** to match your ERP's import schema.\n- Send the alert to email or Microsoft Teams instead of Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0102-4000-8000-000000000102",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        260,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 1. Verify it came from Shopify\n**Raw Body** is on, so the signature is computed over the exact bytes Shopify signed. A request whose HMAC doesn't match gets a 401 and never reaches the ERP."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0103-4000-8000-000000000103",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1040,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 2. Map, queue, then acknowledge\nJitterflow accepts the order instantly, keyed `shopify-order-<id>`. Shopify gets its 200 only after that, so if the hand-off fails, Shopify retries it.\n\nTo pace each store separately, set **Target Identifier** to `{{ $json.shop }}`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0104-4000-8000-000000000104",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        260,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## 3. Each morning, find orders the ERP rejected\nAfter its last retry, Jitterflow moves an order to the DLQ. Only entries whose payload has `source: shopify` are kept, so other endpoints don't show up here."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0105-4000-8000-000000000105",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1040,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## 4. Post one Slack summary\nAll failed orders go into one message with the ERP's status code. Fix the cause, then replay them from the Jitterflow dashboard (replay needs the Pro plan)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Shopify order created",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        320,
        260
      ],
      "webhookId": "d4d4d4d4-00ff-4000-8000-0000000000ff",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "shopify-order-created",
        "options": {
          "rawBody": true
        },
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "responseMode": "responseNode"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Compute signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.crypto",
      "position": [
        520,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "type": "SHA256",
        "action": "hmac",
        "encoding": "base64",
        "binaryData": true,
        "dataPropertyName": "computedHmac"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "crypto": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "Shopify webhook secret"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Signature matches?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        720,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0201-4+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.computedHmac }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-shopify-hmac-sha256'] }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0004-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Reject unsigned request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "position": [
        900,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 401
        },
        "respondWith": "noData"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0005-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Map order to ERP format",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        1100,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0301-4+1234567890",
              "name": "source",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "shopify"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0302-4+1234567890",
              "name": "externalOrderId",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.id }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0303-4+1234567890",
              "name": "orderNumber",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.name }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0304-4+1234567890",
              "name": "shop",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.headers['x-shopify-shop-domain'] }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0305-4+1234567890",
              "name": "placedAt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.created_at }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0306-4+1234567890",
              "name": "currency",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.currency }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0307-4+1234567890",
              "name": "total",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "={{ Number($json.body.total_price) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0308-4+1234567890",
              "name": "customer",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "={{ { email: $json.body.email, name: [$json.body.customer?.first_name, $json.body.customer?.last_name].filter(Boolean).join(' ') } }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-0309-4+1234567890",
              "name": "shipTo",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.shipping_address ? { name: $json.body.shipping_address.name, address1: $json.body.shipping_address.address1, address2: $json.body.shipping_address.address2, city: $json.body.shipping_address.city, region: $json.body.shipping_address.province_code, postalCode: $json.body.shipping_address.zip, country: $json.body.shipping_address.country_code } : {} }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "d4d4d4d4-030a-4+1234567890a",
              "name": "lines",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.line_items.map(line => ({ sku: line.sku, title: line.title, quantity: line.quantity, unitPrice: Number(line.price) })) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Queue order for the ERP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-jitterflow.jitterflow",
      "position": [
        1320,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "payload": "={{ $json }}",
        "resource": "webhook",
        "operation": "send",
